# Finding a shared property value
#
# Alice and Bob are both human. A backward N3 rule calls two subjects
# similar when they share a predicate and object, allowing a forward rule
# to confirm their similarity.

@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/ns#> .
@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#> .

:Alice a :Human .
:Bob a :Human .

{
    :Alice :similar :Bob .
} => {
    :test :is true .
} .

{
    ?A :similar ?B .
} <= {
    ?A ?Pred ?Obj .
    ?B ?Pred ?Obj .
} .
